(169,2,69,'paragraph',NULL,'Alimentary canal is complete with a well-developed muscular pharynx. An excretory tube removes body wastes from the body cavity through the excretory pore. Sexes are separate (dioecious), i.e., males and females are distinct. Often females are longer than males. Fertilisation is internal and development may be direct (the young ones resemble the adult) or indirect.','[{"s": "Alimentary canal is complete with a well-developed muscular pharynx. An excretory tube removes body wastes from the body cavity through the excretory pore.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Sexes are separate (dioecious), i.e., males and females are distinct.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "Often females are longer than males. Fertilisation is internal and development may be direct (the young ones resemble the adult) or indirect.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["40969"]',NULL),
