(559,5,81,'heading',4,'9.12.1 Chemical Reactions',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(560,5,82,'paragraph',NULL,'How do we understand these enzymes? Let us first understand a chemical reaction. Chemical compounds undergo two types of changes. A physical change simply refers to a change in shape without breaking of bonds. This is a physical process. Another physical process is a change in state of matter: when ice melts into water, or when water becomes a vapour. These are also physical processes. However, when bonds are broken and new bonds are formed during transformation, this will be called a chemical reaction. For example:','[{"s": "How do we understand these enzymes? Let us first understand a chemical reaction. Chemical compounds undergo two types of changes. A physical change simply refers to a change in shape without breaking of bonds. This is a physical process. Another physical process is a change in state of matter: when ice melts into water, or when water becomes a vapour. These are also physical processes. However, when bonds are broken and new bonds are formed during transformation, this will be called a chemical reaction. For example:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(561,5,83,'paragraph',NULL,'Ba(OH) 2 + H 2 SO4 → BaSO4 + 2H 2 O','[{"s": "Ba(OH)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "SO4 → BaSO4 + 2H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "O", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(562,5,84,'paragraph',NULL,'is an inorganic chemical reaction. Similarly, hydrolysis of starch into glucose is an organic chemical reaction. Rate of a physical or chemical process refers to the amount of product formed per unit time. It can be expressed as:','[{"s": "is an inorganic chemical reaction. Similarly, hydrolysis of starch into glucose is an organic chemical reaction. Rate of a physical or chemical process refers to the amount of product formed per unit time. It can be expressed as:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(563,5,85,'paragraph',NULL,'rate = Biomolecules-image4.png','[{"s": "rate =", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Biomolecules-image4.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(564,5,86,'paragraph',NULL,'Rate can also be called velocity if the direction is specified. Rates of physical and chemical processes are influenced by temperature among other factors. A general rule of thumb is that rate doubles or decreases by half for every 10°C change in either direction. Catalysed reactions proceed at rates vastly higher than that of uncatalysed ones. When enzyme catalysed reactions are observed, the rate would be vastly higher than the same but uncatalysed reaction. For example','[{"s": "Rate can also be called velocity if the direction is specified. Rates of physical and chemical processes are influenced by temperature among other factors. A general rule of thumb is that rate doubles or decreases by half for every 10°C change in either direction. Catalysed reactions proceed at rates vastly higher than that of uncatalysed ones. When enzyme catalysed reactions are observed, the rate would be vastly higher than the same but uncatalysed reaction. For example", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(565,5,87,'paragraph',NULL,'CO 2 + H 2 O Biomolecules-image5.png H 2 CO carbonic acid','[{"s": "CO", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Biomolecules-image5.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "CO", "t": "text"}, {"s": "carbonic acid", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(566,5,88,'paragraph',NULL,'In the absence of any enzyme this reaction is very slow, with about 200 molecules of H 2 CO 3 being formed in an hour. However, by using the enzyme present within the cytoplasm called carbonic anhydrase, the reaction speeds dramatically with about 600,000 molecules being formed every second. The enzyme has accelerated the reaction rate by about 10 million times. The power of enzymes is incredible indeed!','[{"s": "In the absence of any enzyme this reaction is very slow, with about 200 molecules of H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "CO", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "being formed in an hour. However, by using the enzyme present within the cytoplasm called carbonic anhydrase, the reaction speeds dramatically with about 600,000 molecules being formed every second. The enzyme has accelerated the reaction rate by about 10 million times. The power of enzymes is incredible indeed!", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(567,5,89,'paragraph',NULL,'There are thousands of types of enzymes each catalysing a unique chemical or metabolic reaction. A multistep chemical reaction, when each of the steps is catalysed by the same enzyme complex or different enzymes, is called a metabolic pathway. For example,','[{"s": "There are thousands of types of enzymes each catalysing a unique chemical or metabolic reaction. A multistep chemical reaction, when each of the steps is catalysed by the same enzyme complex or different enzymes, is called a metabolic pathway. For example,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
