(822,8,18,'paragraph',NULL,'Figure 18.1 Diagrammatic representation of formed elements in blood','[{"s": "Figure 18.1 Diagrammatic representation of formed elements in blood", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["181638"]',NULL),
(823,8,19,'paragraph',NULL,'Platelets also called thrombocytes, are cell fragments produced from megakaryocytes (special cells in the bone marrow). Blood normally contains 1,500,00-3,500,00 platelets mm –3 . Platelets can release a variety of substances most of which are involved in the coagulation or clotting of blood. A reduction in their number can lead to clotting disorders which will lead to excessive loss of blood from the body.','[{"s": "Platelets also called thrombocytes, are cell fragments produced from megakaryocytes (special cells in the bone marrow). Blood normally contains 1,500,00-3,500,00 platelets mm", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–3", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Platelets can release a variety of substances most of which are involved in the coagulation or clotting of blood.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "A reduction in their number can lead to clotting disorders which will lead to excessive loss of blood from the body.", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["181627", "181635", "181702"]',NULL),
(824,8,20,'heading',4,'18.1.3 Blood Groups',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(825,8,21,'paragraph',NULL,'As you know, blood of human beings differ in certain aspects though it appears to be similar. Various types of grouping of blood has been done. Two such groupings – the ABO and Rh – are widely used all over the world.','[{"s": "As you know, blood of human beings differ in certain aspects though it appears to be similar. Various types of grouping of blood has been done. Two such groupings – the ABO and Rh – are widely used all over the world.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(826,8,22,'paragraph',NULL,'18.1.3.1 ABO grouping','[{"s": "18.1.3.1 ABO grouping", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(829,8,25,'image',NULL,'p3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/biology/images/Body_Fluids_and_Circulation-image3.png'),
(830,8,26,'paragraph',NULL,'From the above mentioned table it is evident that group ‘O’ blood can be donated to persons with any other blood group and hence ‘O’ group individuals are called ‘universal donors’. Persons with ‘AB’ group can accept blood from persons with AB as well as the other groups of blood. T herefore, such persons are called ‘universal recipients’.','[{"s": "From the above mentioned table it is evident that group ‘O’ blood can be donated to persons with any other blood group and hence ‘O’ group individuals are called ‘universal donors’. Persons with ‘AB’ group can accept blood from persons with AB as well as the other groups of blood. T", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "herefore, such persons are called ‘universal recipients’.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["181502", "181521", "181609", "181624", "181626"]',NULL),
(831,8,27,'paragraph',NULL,'18.1.3.2 Rh grouping','[{"s": "18.1.3.2 Rh grouping", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
