(1183,12,25,'heading',4,'22.2.3 The Pineal Gland',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(1184,12,26,'paragraph',NULL,'The pineal gland is located on the dorsal side of forebrain. Pineal secretes a hormone called melatonin . Melatonin plays a very important role in the regulation of a 24-hour (diurnal) rhythm of our body. For example, it helps in maintaining the normal rhythms of sleep-wake cycle, body temperature. In addition, melatonin also influences metabolism, pigmentation, the menstrual cycle as well as our defense capability.','[{"s": "The pineal gland is located on the dorsal side of forebrain. Pineal secretes a hormone called", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "melatonin", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ". Melatonin plays a very important role in the regulation of a 24-hour (diurnal) rhythm of our body. For example, it helps in maintaining the normal rhythms of sleep-wake cycle, body temperature.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "In addition, melatonin also influences metabolism, pigmentation, the menstrual cycle as well as our defense capability.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["221619", "221716"]',NULL),
