(1995,20,126,'heading',3,'6.5.2 Transcription Unit and the Gene',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(1997,20,128,'paragraph',NULL,'Inheritance of a character is also affected by promoter and regulatory sequences of a structural gene. Hence, sometime the regulatory sequences are loosely defined as regulatory genes, even though these sequences do not code for any RNA or protein.','[{"s": "Inheritance of a character is also affected by promoter and regulatory sequences of a structural gene. Hence, sometime the regulatory sequences are loosely defined as regulatory genes, even though these sequences do not code for any RNA or protein.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(1998,20,129,'heading',3,'6.5.3 Types of RNA and the process of Transcription',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(1999,20,130,'paragraph',NULL,'In bacteria, there are three major types of RNAs: mRNA (messenger RNA), tRNA (transfer RNA), and rRNA (ribosomal RNA). All three RNAs are needed to synthesise a protein in a cell. The mRNA provides the template, tRNA brings aminoacids and reads the genetic code, and rRNAs play structural and catalytic role during translation.','[{"s": "In bacteria, there are three major types of RNAs: mRNA (messenger RNA), tRNA (transfer RNA), and rRNA (ribosomal RNA). All three RNAs are needed to synthesise a protein in a cell. The mRNA provides the template, tRNA brings aminoacids and reads the genetic code, and rRNAs play structural and catalytic role during translation.", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["282711"]',NULL),
(2000,20,131,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/biology/images/Molecular_Basis_of_Inheritance-image16.png'),
(2001,20,132,'paragraph',NULL,'Figure 6.10 Process of Transcription in Bacteria','[{"s": "Figure 6.10 Process of Transcription in Bacteria", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(2004,20,135,'paragraph',NULL,'In bacteria, since the mRNA does not require any processing to become active, and also since transcription and translation take place in the same compartment (there is no separation of cytosol and nucleus in bacteria), many times the translation can begin much before the mRNA is fully transcribed. Consequently, the transcription and translation can be coupled in bacteria.','[{"s": "In bacteria, since the mRNA does not require any processing to become active, and also since transcription and translation take place in the same compartment (there is no separation of cytosol and nucleus in bacteria), many times the translation can begin much before the mRNA is fully transcribed. Consequently, the transcription and translation can be coupled in bacteria.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(2005,20,136,'paragraph',NULL,'In eukaryotes, there are two additional complexities –','[{"s": "In eukaryotes, there are two additional complexities –", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
