(2546,23,107,'paragraph',NULL,'The above equation describes the exponential or geometric growth pattern of a population (Figure 13.6) and results in a J-shaped curve when we plot N in relation to time . If you are familiar with basic calculus, you can derive the integral form of the exponential growth equation as','[{"s": "The above equation describes the exponential or geometric growth pattern of a population (Figure 13.6) and results in a J-shaped curve when we plot N in relation to time", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". If you are familiar with basic calculus, you can derive the integral form of the exponential growth equation as", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
