(7752,39,472,'paragraph',NULL,'30. Choose the correct order of atomic radii of fluorine and neon (in pm) out of the options given below and justify your answer.','[{"s": "30. Choose the correct order of atomic radii of fluorine and neon (in pm) out of the options given below and justify your answer.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(3235,27,158,'paragraph',NULL,'Colour Blidness : It is a sex-linked recessive disorder due to defect in either red or green cone of eye resulting in failure to discriminate between red and green colour. This defect is due to mutation in certain genes present in the X chromosome. It occurs in about 8 per cent of males and only about 0.4 per cent of females. This is because the genes that lead to red-green colour blindness are on the X chromosome. Males have only one X chromosome and females have two. The son of a woman who carries the gene has a 50 per cent chance of being colour blind. The mother is not herself colour blind because the gene is recessive. That means that its effect is suppressed by her matching dominant normal gene. A daughter will not normally be colour blind, unless her mother is a carrier and her father is colour blind.','[{"s": "Colour Blidness", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ": It is a sex-linked recessive disorder due to defect in either red or green cone of eye resulting in failure to discriminate between red and green colour.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "This defect is due to mutation in certain genes present in the X chromosome. It occurs in about 8 per cent of males and only about 0.4 per cent of females.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "This is because the genes that lead to red-green colour blindness are on the X chromosome.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Males have only one X chromosome and females have two. The son of a woman who carries the gene has a 50 per cent chance of being colour blind. The mother is not herself colour blind because the gene is recessive. That means that its effect is suppressed by her matching dominant normal gene. A daughter will not normally be colour blind, unless her mother is a carrier and her father is colour blind.", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["271702", "271704", "271706", "271795", "271796", "271797"]',NULL),
(3237,27,160,'paragraph',NULL,'The family pedigree of Queen Victoria shows a number of haemophilic descendents as she was a carrier of the disease.','[{"s": "The family pedigree of Queen Victoria shows a number of haemophilic descendents as she was a carrier of the disease.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(3238,27,161,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/biology/images/Principles_Of_Inheritance_And_Variation-image11.png'),
(3239,27,162,'paragraph',NULL,'Figure 5.15 Micrograph of the red blood cells and the amino acid composition of the relevant portion of β-chain of haemoglobin: (a) From a normal individual; (b) From an individual with sickle-cell anaemia','[{"s": "Figure 5.15", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Micrograph of the red blood cells and the amino acid composition of the relevant portion of β-chain of haemoglobin: (a) From a normal individual; (b) From an individual with sickle-cell anaemia", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(3241,27,164,'paragraph',NULL,'Phenylketonuria : This inborn error of metabolism is also inherited as the autosomal recessive trait. The affected individual lacks an enzyme that converts the amino acid phenylalanine into tyrosine. As a result of this phenylalanine is accumulated and converted into phenylpyruvic acid and other derivatives. Accumulation of these in brain results in mental retardation. These are also excreted through urine because of its poor absorption by kidney.','[{"s": "Phenylketonuria :", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "This inborn error of metabolism is also inherited as the autosomal recessive trait.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "The affected individual lacks an enzyme that converts the amino acid phenylalanine into tyrosine. As a result of this phenylalanine is accumulated and converted into phenylpyruvic acid and other derivatives. Accumulation of these in brain results in mental retardation. These are also excreted through urine because of its poor absorption by kidney.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["271719", "271779", "271782"]',NULL),
