(6381,37,513,'paragraph',NULL,'2 HI(g) → H 2 + I 2 (g)','[{"s": "2 HI(g) → H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+ I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(g)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(33774,78,335,'paragraph',NULL,'= 373.7 m 3','[{"s": "= 373.7 m", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4286,34,350,'paragraph',NULL,'Ethers are the least reactive of the functional groups. The cleavage of C-O bond in ethers takes place under drastic conditions with excess of hydrogen halides. 3 The reaction of dialkyl ether gives two alkyl halide molecules.','[{"s": "Ethers are the least reactive of the functional groups.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "The cleavage of C-O bond in ethers takes place under drastic conditions with excess of hydrogen halides.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "3", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "The reaction of dialkyl ether gives two alkyl halide molecules.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["250916", "250950", "250987", "250988"]',NULL),
(4287,34,351,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image37.png'),
(4288,34,352,'paragraph',NULL,'Alkyl aryl ethers are cleaved at the alkyl-oxygen bond due to the more stable aryl-oxygen bond. The reaction yields phenol and alkyl halide.','[{"s": "Alkyl aryl ethers are cleaved at the alkyl-oxygen bond due to the more stable aryl-oxygen bond.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "The reaction yields phenol and alkyl halide.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["250989"]',NULL),
(4289,34,353,'image',NULL,'Img20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image86.png'),
(4290,34,354,'paragraph',NULL,'Ethers with two different alkyl groups are also cleaved in the same manner.','[{"s": "Ethers with two different alkyl groups are also cleaved in the same manner.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4291,34,355,'image',NULL,'Img21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image162.png'),
(4292,34,356,'paragraph',NULL,'Mechanism','[{"s": "Mechanism", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4293,34,357,'paragraph',NULL,'The reaction of an ether with concentrated HI starts with protonation of ether molecule.','[{"s": "The reaction of an ether with concentrated HI starts with protonation of ether molecule.", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["250990"]',NULL),
(4294,34,358,'paragraph',NULL,'Step 1: Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image63.png','[{"s": "Step 1:", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image63.png", "t": "img", "alt": "Img22"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4295,34,359,'paragraph',NULL,'The reaction takes place with HBr or HI because these reagents are sufficiently acidic.','[{"s": "The reaction takes place with HBr or HI because these reagents are sufficiently acidic.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4296,34,360,'paragraph',NULL,'Step 2:','[{"s": "Step 2:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4297,34,361,'paragraph',NULL,'Iodide is a good nucleophile. It attacks the least substituted carbon of the oxonium ion formed in step 1 and displaces an alcohol molecule by S n 2 mechanism.','[{"s": "Iodide is a good nucleophile. It attacks the least substituted carbon of the oxonium ion formed in step 1 and displaces an alcohol molecule by S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "n", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2 mechanism.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4298,34,362,'paragraph',NULL,'Thus, in the cleavage of mixed ethers with two different alkyl groups, the alcohol and alkyl iodide formed, depend on the nature of alkyl groups. When primary or secondary alkyl groups are present, it is the lower alkyl group that forms alkyl iodide (S n 2 reaction).','[{"s": "Thus, in the cleavage of mixed ethers with two different alkyl groups, the alcohol and alkyl iodide formed, depend on the nature of alkyl groups.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "When primary or secondary alkyl groups are present, it is the lower alkyl group that forms alkyl iodide (S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "n", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2 reaction).", "t": "text"}]','marked','["250909"]',NULL),
(4299,34,363,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image60.png'),
(4300,34,364,'paragraph',NULL,'When HI is in excess and the reaction is carried out at high temperature, ethanol reacts with another molecule of HI and is converted to ethyl iodide.','[{"s": "When HI is in excess and the reaction is carried out at high temperature, ethanol reacts with another molecule of HI and is converted to ethyl iodide.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4301,34,365,'paragraph',NULL,'Step 3:','[{"s": "Step 3:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4302,34,366,'image',NULL,'Img24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image116.png'),
(4303,34,367,'paragraph',NULL,'However, when one of the alkyl group is a tertiary group, the halide formed is a tertiary halide.','[{"s": "However, when one of the alkyl group is a tertiary group, the halide formed is a tertiary halide.", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["250956"]',NULL),
(4304,34,368,'image',NULL,'Img25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image28.png'),
(4305,34,369,'paragraph',NULL,'It is because in step 2 of the reaction, the departure of leaving group (HO–CH 3 ) creates a more stable carbocation [(CH 3 ) 3 C + ], and the reaction follows S n 1 mechanism.','[{"s": "It is because in step 2 of the reaction, the departure of leaving group (HO–CH", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") creates a more stable carbocation [(CH", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+", "t": "text"}, {"s": "], and the reaction follows S", "t": "text"}, {"s": "n", "t": "text"}, {"s": "1 mechanism.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4306,34,370,'paragraph',NULL,'In case of anisole, methylphenyl oxonium ion, Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image31.png is formed by protonation of ether. The bond between O–CH 3 is weaker than the bond between O–C 6 H 5 because the carbon of phenyl group is sp 2 hybridised and there is a partial double bond character.','[{"s": "In case of anisole, methylphenyl oxonium ion,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image31.png", "t": "img", "alt": "Img26"}, {"s": "is formed by protonation of ether. The bond between O–CH", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is weaker than the bond between O–C", "t": "text"}, {"s": "6", "t": "text"}, {"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "5", "t": "text"}, {"s": "because the carbon of phenyl group is sp", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "hybridised and there is a partial double bond character.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4307,34,371,'image',NULL,'Img27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image107.png'),
(6382,37,514,'paragraph',NULL,'is 209.5 kJ mol –1 at 581K.Calculate the fraction of molecules of reactants having energy equal to or greater than activation energy?','[{"s": "is 209.5 kJ mol", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "at 581K.Calculate the fraction of molecules of reactants having energy equal to or greater than activation energy?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(6383,37,515,'heading',3,'Summary',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(12630,44,1400,'paragraph',NULL,'Q.28 Haloalkanes_and_Haloarenes-image74.png','[{"s": "Q.28", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Haloalkanes_and_Haloarenes-image74.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4308,34,372,'paragraph',NULL,'Therefore the attack by I – ion breaks O–CH 3 bond to form CH 3 I. Phenols do not react further to give halides because the sp 2 hybridised carbon of phenol cannot undergo nucleophilic substitution reaction needed for conversion to the halide.','[{"s": "Therefore the attack by I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ion breaks O–CH", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "bond to form CH", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "I. Phenols do not react further to give halides because the sp", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "hybridised carbon of phenol cannot undergo nucleophilic substitution reaction needed for conversion to the halide.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4309,34,373,'paragraph',NULL,'Example 11.7','[{"s": "Example 11.7", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4310,34,374,'paragraph',NULL,'Give the major products that are formed by heating each of the following ethers with HI.','[{"s": "Give the major products that are formed by heating each of the following ethers with HI.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(4311,34,375,'image',NULL,'Img28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Alcohols_Phenols_and_Ethers-image35.png'),
