(5900,37,32,'paragraph',NULL,'Units of rate of a reaction','[{"s": "Units of rate of a reaction", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(5901,37,33,'paragraph',NULL,'From equations (4.1) and (4.2), it is clear that units of rate are concentration time –1 . For example, if concentration is in mol L –1 and time is in seconds then the units will be mol L -1 s –1 . However, in gaseous reactions, when the concentration of gases is expressed in terms of their partial pressures, then the units of the rate equation will be atm s –1 .','[{"s": "From equations (4.1) and (4.2), it is clear that units of rate are concentration time", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". For example, if concentration is in mol L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and time is in seconds then the units will be mol L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "-1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". However, in gaseous reactions, when the concentration of gases is expressed in terms of their partial pressures, then the units of the rate equation will be atm s", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ".", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL);
