(5926,37,58,'paragraph',NULL,'i.e., rate of disappearance of any of the reactants is same as the rate of appearance of the products. But in the following reaction, two moles of HI decompose to produce one mole each of H 2 and I 2,','[{"s": "i.e., rate of disappearance of any of the reactants is same as the rate of appearance of the products. But in the following reaction, two moles of HI decompose to produce one mole each of H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(5927,37,59,'paragraph',NULL,'2HI(g) → H 2 (g) + I 2 (g)','[{"s": "2HI(g) → H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(g) + I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(g)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(5928,37,60,'paragraph',NULL,'For expressing the rate of such a reaction where stoichiometric coefficients of reactants or products are not equal to one, rate of disappearance of any of the reactants or the rate of appearance of products is divided by their respective stoichiometric coefficients. 2 Since rate of consumption of HI is twice the rate of formation of H 2 or I 2 , to make them equal, the term ∆[HI] is divided by 2. The rate of this reaction is given by','[{"s": "For expressing the rate of such a reaction where stoichiometric coefficients of reactants or products are not equal to one, rate of disappearance of any of the reactants or the rate of appearance of products is divided by their respective stoichiometric coefficients.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "2", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "Since rate of consumption of HI is twice the rate of formation of H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "or I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", to make them equal, the term ∆[HI] is divided by 2. The rate of this reaction is given by", "t": "text"}]','marked','["181004", "181007"]',NULL),
