(6200,37,332,'paragraph',NULL,'It can be seen that for a first order reaction, half-life period is constant, i.e., it is independent of initial concentration of the reacting species. The half-life of a first order equation is readily calculated from the rate constant and vice versa.','[{"s": "It can be seen that for a first order reaction, half-life period is constant, i.e., it is independent of initial concentration of the reacting species.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The half-life of a first order equation is readily calculated from the rate constant and vice versa.", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["181035"]',NULL),
