(7314,39,34,'heading',3,'3.3 MODERN PERIODIC LAW AND THE PRESENT FORM OF THE PERIODIC TABLE',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(7315,39,35,'paragraph',NULL,'We must bear in mind that when Mendeleev developed his Periodic Table , chemists knew nothing about the internal structure of atom. However, the beginning of the 20 th century witnessed profound developments in theories about sub-atomic particles. In 1913, the English physicist, Henry Moseley observed regularities in the characteristic X-ray spectra of the elements. A plot of Classification_of_Elements_and_Periodicity_in_Properties-image5.png (where Classification_of_Elements_and_Periodicity_in_Properties-image16.png is frequency of X-rays emitted) against atomic number (Z ) gave a straight line and not the plot of Classification_of_Elements_and_Periodicity_in_Properties-image5.png vs atomic mass. He thereby showed that the atomic number is a more fundamental property of an element than its atomic mass. Mendeleev’s Periodic Law was, therefore, accordingly modified. This is known as the Modern Periodic Law and can be stated as :','[{"s": "We must bear in mind that when Mendeleev developed his", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Periodic Table", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", chemists knew nothing about the internal structure of atom. However, the beginning of the 20", "t": "text"}, {"s": "th", "t": "text"}, {"s": "century witnessed profound developments in theories about sub-atomic particles. In 1913, the English physicist, Henry Moseley observed regularities in the characteristic X-ray spectra of the elements. A plot of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Classification_of_Elements_and_Periodicity_in_Properties-image5.png", "t": "img", "alt": "Screenshot from 2019-06-03 17-58-47"}, {"s": "(where", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Classification_of_Elements_and_Periodicity_in_Properties-image16.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "is frequency of X-rays emitted) against atomic number (Z ) gave a straight line and not the plot of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Classification_of_Elements_and_Periodicity_in_Properties-image5.png", "t": "img", "alt": "Screenshot from 2019-06-03 17-58-47"}, {"s": "vs atomic mass. He thereby showed that the atomic number is a more fundamental property of an element than its atomic mass.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Mendeleev’s Periodic Law", "t": "text"}, {"s": "was, therefore, accordingly modified. This is known as the", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Modern Periodic Law", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and can be stated as :", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(7316,39,36,'paragraph',NULL,'The physical and chemical properties of the elements are periodic functions of their atomic numbers.','[{"s": "The physical and chemical properties of the elements are periodic functions of their atomic numbers.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(7317,39,37,'paragraph',NULL,'The Periodic Law revealed important analogies among the 94 naturally occurring elements (neptunium and plutonium like actinium and protoactinium are also found in pitch blende – an ore of uranium). It stimulated renewed interest in Inorganic Chemistry and has carried into the present with the creation of artificially produced short-lived elements.','[{"s": "The", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Periodic Law", "t": "text"}, {"s": "revealed important analogies among the 94 naturally occurring elements (neptunium and plutonium like actinium and protoactinium are also found in pitch blende – an ore of uranium). It stimulated renewed interest in Inorganic Chemistry and has carried into the present with the creation of artificially produced short-lived elements.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(7318,39,38,'paragraph',NULL,'You may recall that the atomic number is equal to the nuclear charge (i.e., number of protons) or the number of electrons in a neutral atom. It is then easy to visualize the significance of quantum numbers and electronic configurations in periodicity of elements. In fact, it is now recognized that the Periodic Law is essentially the consequence of the periodic variation in electronic configurations, which indeed determine the physical and chemical properties of elements and their compounds.','[{"s": "You may recall that the atomic number is equal to the nuclear charge (i.e., number of protons) or the number of electrons in a neutral atom. It is then easy to visualize the significance of quantum numbers and electronic configurations in periodicity of elements. In fact, it is now recognized that the Periodic Law is essentially the consequence of the periodic variation in electronic configurations, which indeed determine the physical and chemical properties of elements and their compounds.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(7319,39,39,'paragraph',NULL,'Numerous forms of Periodic Table have been devised from time to time. Some forms emphasise chemical reactions and valence, whereas others stress the electronic configuration of elements. A modern version, the so-called “ long form ” of the Periodic Table of the elements (Fig. 3.2), is the most convenient and widely used. The horizontal rows (which Mendeleev called series ) are called periods and the vertical columns, groups . Elements having similar outer electronic configurations in their atoms are arranged in vertical columns, referred to as groups or families . According to the recommendation of International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry (IUPAC), the groups are numbered from 1 to 18 replacing the older notation of groups IA … VIIA, VIII, IB … VIIB and 0.','[{"s": "Numerous forms of Periodic Table have been devised from time to time. Some forms emphasise chemical reactions and valence, whereas others stress the electronic configuration of elements. A modern version, the so-called “", "t": "text"}, {"s": "long form", "t": "text"}, {"s": "” of the", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Periodic Table", "t": "text"}, {"s": "of the elements (Fig. 3.2), is the most convenient and widely used. The horizontal rows (which Mendeleev called", "t": "text"}, {"s": "series", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") are called", "t": "text"}, {"s": "periods", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and the vertical columns,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "groups", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Elements having similar outer electronic configurations in their atoms are arranged in vertical columns, referred to as", "t": "text"}, {"s": "groups", "t": "text"}, {"s": "or", "t": "text"}, {"s": "families", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". According to the recommendation of International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry (IUPAC), the groups are numbered from 1 to 18 replacing the older notation of groups IA … VIIA, VIII, IB … VIIB and 0.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(12203,44,973,'paragraph',NULL,'. Which of the following species attacks the benzene','[{"s": ". Which of the following species attacks the benzene", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
