(9231,42,9,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig. 3.1: Daniell cell having electrodes of zinc and copper dipping in the solutions of their respective salts.','[{"s": "Fig. 3.1: Daniell cell having electrodes of zinc and copper dipping in the solutions of their respective salts.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(9232,42,10,'paragraph',NULL,'Electrochemistry-image75.png Fig. 3.2 Functioning of Daniell cell when external voltage Eext opposing the cell potential is applied.','[{"s": "Electrochemistry-image75.png", "t": "img", "alt": "3a"}, {"s": "Fig. 3.2 Functioning of Daniell cell when external voltage Eext opposing the cell potential is applied.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(9233,42,11,'paragraph',NULL,'If an external opposite potential is applied in the galvanic cell [Fig. 3.2(a)] and increased slowly, we find that the reaction continues to take place till the opposing voltage reaches the value 1.1 V [Fig. 3.2(b)] when, the reaction stops altogether and no current flows through the cell. Any further increase in the external potential again starts the reaction but in the opposite direction [Fig. 3.2(c)]. It now functions as an electrolytic cell , a device for using electrical energy to carry non-spontaneous chemical reactions. Both types of cells are quite important and we shall study some of their salient features in the following pages.','[{"s": "If an external opposite potential is applied in the galvanic cell [Fig. 3.2(a)] and increased slowly, we find that the reaction continues to take place till the opposing voltage reaches the value 1.1 V [Fig. 3.2(b)] when, the reaction stops altogether and no current flows through the cell. Any further increase in the external potential again starts the reaction but in the opposite direction [Fig. 3.2(c)]. It now functions as an", "t": "text"}, {"s": "electrolytic", "t": "text"}, {"s": "cell", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", a device for using electrical energy to carry non-spontaneous chemical reactions. Both types of cells are quite important and we shall study some of their salient features in the following pages.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(9234,42,12,'paragraph',NULL,'*Strictly speaking activity should be used instead of concentration. It is directly proportional to concentration. In dilute solutions, it is equal to concentration. You will study more about it in higher classes.','[{"s": "*Strictly speaking activity should be used instead of concentration. It is directly proportional to concentration. In dilute solutions, it is equal to concentration. You will study more about it in higher classes.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(9235,42,13,'heading',3,'3.2 Galvanic Cells',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(9236,42,14,'paragraph',NULL,'As mentioned earlier (Class XI, Unit 8) a galvanic cell is an electrochemical cell that converts the chemical energy of a spontaneous redox reaction into electrical energy. In this device the Gibbs energy of the spontaneous redox reaction is converted into electrical work which may be used for running a motor or other electrical gadgets like heater, fan, geyser, etc.','[{"s": "As mentioned earlier (Class XI, Unit 8) a galvanic cell is an electrochemical cell that converts the chemical energy of a spontaneous redox reaction into electrical energy. In this device the", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Gibbs energy", "t": "text"}, {"s": "of the spontaneous redox reaction is converted into electrical work which may be used for running a motor or other electrical gadgets like heater, fan, geyser, etc.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(9237,42,15,'paragraph',NULL,'Daniell cell discussed earlier is one such cell in which the following redox reaction occurs.','[{"s": "Daniell cell discussed earlier is one such cell in which the following redox reaction occurs.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
