(9357,42,135,'paragraph',NULL,'Electrical work done in one second is equal to electrical potential multiplied by total charge passed. If we want to obtain maximum work from a galvanic cell then charge has to be passed reversibly. The reversible work done by a galvanic cell is equal to decrease in its Gibbs energy and therefore, if the emf of the cell is E and nF is the amount of charge passed and ∆ r G is the Gibbs energy of the reaction, then','[{"s": "Electrical work done in one second is equal to electrical potential multiplied by total charge passed.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "If we want to obtain maximum work from a galvanic cell then charge has to be passed reversibly. The reversible work done by a galvanic cell is equal to decrease in its Gibbs energy and therefore, if the emf of the cell is", "t": "text"}, {"s": "E", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "nF", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the amount of charge passed and ∆", "t": "text"}, {"s": "r", "t": "text"}, {"s": "G", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is the Gibbs energy of the reaction, then", "t": "text"}]','marked','["171122"]',NULL),
