(9540,42,318,'paragraph',NULL,'3.9 The molar conductivity of 0.025 mol L –1 methanoic acid is 46.1 S cm 2 mol –1 . Calculate its degree of dissociation and dissociation constant. Given λ°(H + ) = 349.6 S cm 2 mol –1 and λ° (HCOO – ) = 54.6 S cm 2','[{"s": "3.9", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The molar conductivity of 0.025 mol L", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "methanoic acid is 46.1 S cm", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "mol", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Calculate its degree of dissociation and dissociation constant. Given λ°(H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") = 349.6 S cm", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "mol", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–1", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and λ° (HCOO", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") = 54.6 S cm", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
