(10465,43,451,'heading',3,'7.8 FACTORS AFFECTING EQUILIBRIA',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10466,43,452,'paragraph',NULL,'One of the principal goals of chemical synthesis is to maximise the conversion of the reactants to products while minimizing the expenditure of energy. This implies maximum yield of products at mild temperature and pressure conditions. If it does not happen, then the experimental conditions need to be adjusted. For example, in the Haber process for the synthesis of ammonia from N 2 and H 2 , the choice of experimental conditions is of real economic importance. Annual world production of ammonia is about hundred million tones, primarily for use as fertilizers .','[{"s": "One of the principal goals of chemical synthesis is to maximise the conversion of the reactants to products while minimizing the expenditure of energy.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "This implies maximum yield of products at mild temperature and pressure conditions.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "If it does not happen, then the experimental conditions need to be adjusted. For example, in the Haber process for the synthesis of ammonia from N", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", the choice of experimental conditions is of real economic importance.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Annual world production of ammonia is about hundred million tones, primarily for use as fertilizers", "t": "hl"}, {"s": ".", "t": "hl"}]','marked','["71150", "71172"]',NULL),
(12419,44,1189,'paragraph',NULL,'C','[{"s": "C", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(12420,44,1190,'paragraph',NULL,'H','[{"s": "H", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(12421,44,1191,'paragraph',NULL,'2','[{"s": "2", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(12422,44,1192,'paragraph',NULL,'B','[{"s": "B", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10467,43,453,'paragraph',NULL,'Equilibrium constant, K c is independent of initial concentrations. But if a system at equilibrium is subjected to a change in the concentration of one or more of the reacting substances, then the system is no longer at equilibrium; and net reaction takes place in some direction until the system returns to equilibrium once again. Similarly, a change in temperature or pressure of the system may also alter the equilibrium. In order to decide what course the reaction adopts and make a qualitative prediction about the effect of a change in conditions on equilibrium we use Le Chatelier’s principle. It states that a change in any of the factors that determine the equilibrium conditions of a system will cause the system to change in such a manner so as to reduce or to counteract the effect of the change. This is applicable to all physical and chemical equilibria.','[{"s": "Equilibrium constant,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "c", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is independent of initial concentrations. But if a system at equilibrium is subjected to a change in the concentration of one or more of the reacting substances, then the system is no longer at equilibrium; and net reaction takes place in some direction until the system returns to equilibrium once again. Similarly, a change in temperature or pressure of the system may also alter the equilibrium. In order to decide what course the reaction adopts and", "t": "text"}, {"s": "make a qualitative prediction", "t": "text"}, {"s": "about the effect of a change in conditions on equilibrium we use Le Chatelier’s principle. It states that a", "t": "text"}, {"s": "change in any of the factors that determine the equilibrium conditions of a system will cause the system to change in such a manner so as to reduce or to counteract the effect of the change.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "This is applicable to all physical and chemical equilibria.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10468,43,454,'paragraph',NULL,'We shall now be discussing factors which can influence the equilibrium.','[{"s": "We shall now be discussing factors which can influence the equilibrium.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10469,43,455,'heading',4,'7.8.1 Effect of Concentration Change',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10470,43,456,'paragraph',NULL,'In general, when equilibrium is disturbed by the addition/removal of any reactant/products, Le Chatelier’s principle predicts that:','[{"s": "In general, when equilibrium is disturbed by the addition/removal of any reactant/products, Le Chatelier’s principle predicts that:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10471,43,457,'paragraph',NULL,'• The concentration stress of an added reactant/product is relieved by net reaction in the direction that consumes the added substance.','[{"s": "• The concentration stress of an", "t": "text"}, {"s": "added", "t": "text"}, {"s": "reactant/product is relieved by net reaction in the direction that consumes the added substance.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10472,43,458,'paragraph',NULL,'• The concentration stress of a removed reactant/product is relieved by net reaction in the direction that replenishes the removed substance.','[{"s": "• The concentration stress of a", "t": "text"}, {"s": "removed", "t": "text"}, {"s": "reactant/product is relieved by net reaction in the direction that", "t": "text"}, {"s": "replenishes", "t": "text"}, {"s": "the removed substance.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10473,43,459,'paragraph',NULL,'or in other words,','[{"s": "or in other words,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10474,43,460,'paragraph',NULL,'“ When the concentration of any of the reactants or products in a reaction at equilibrium is changed, the composition of the equilibrium mixture changes so as to minimize the effect of concentration changes”.','[{"s": "“", "t": "text"}, {"s": "When the concentration of any of the reactants or products in a reaction at equilibrium is changed, the composition of the equilibrium mixture changes so as to minimize the effect of concentration changes”.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10475,43,461,'paragraph',NULL,'Let us take the reaction,','[{"s": "Let us take the reaction,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10476,43,462,'paragraph',NULL,'H 2 (g) + I 2 (g) Equilibrium-image1.png 2HI(g)','[{"s": "H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(g) + I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(g)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Equilibrium-image1.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "2HI(g)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10477,43,463,'paragraph',NULL,'If H 2 is added to the reaction mixture at equilibrium, then the equilibrium of the reaction is disturbed. In order to restore it, the reaction proceeds in a direction wherein H 2 is consumed, i.e., more of H 2 and I 2 react to form HI and finally the equilibrium shifts in right (forward) direction (Fig.7.8). This is in accordance with the Le Chatelier’s principle which implies that in case of addition of a reactant/product, a new equilibrium will be set up in which the concentration of the reactant/product should be less than what it was after the addition but more than what it was in the original mixture.','[{"s": "If H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is added to the reaction mixture at equilibrium, then the equilibrium of the reaction is disturbed. In order to restore it, the reaction proceeds in a direction wherein H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is consumed, i.e., more of H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "react to form HI and finally the equilibrium shifts in right (forward) direction (Fig.7.8). This is in accordance with the Le Chatelier’s principle which implies that in case of addition of a reactant/product, a new equilibrium will be set up in which the concentration of the reactant/product should be less than what it was after the addition but more than what it was in the original mixture.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10478,43,464,'image',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'/ncert/chemistry/images/Equilibrium-image20.png'),
(10479,43,465,'paragraph',NULL,'Fig. 7.8 Effect of addition of H2 on change of concentration for the reactants and products in the reaction,','[{"s": "Fig. 7.8 Effect of addition of H2 on change of concentration for the reactants and products in the reaction,", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10480,43,466,'paragraph',NULL,'H2(g) + I2 (g) Equilibrium-image1.png 2HI(g)','[{"s": "H2(g) + I2 (g)", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Equilibrium-image1.png", "t": "img", "alt": ""}, {"s": "2HI(g)", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10481,43,467,'paragraph',NULL,'The same point can be explained in terms of the reaction quotient, Q c ,','[{"s": "The same point can be explained in terms of the reaction quotient,", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Q", "t": "text"}, {"s": "c", "t": "text"}, {"s": ",", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10482,43,468,'paragraph',NULL,'Q c = [HI] 2 / [H 2 ][I 2 ]','[{"s": "Q", "t": "text"}, {"s": "c", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= [HI]", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "/ [H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "][I", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "]", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(12423,44,1193,'paragraph',NULL,'r','[{"s": "r", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(12424,44,1194,'paragraph',NULL,'∣','[{"s": "∣", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
