(10558,43,544,'paragraph',NULL,'It can be seen in the above equation, that water acts as a base because it accepts the proton. The species H 3 O + is produced when water accepts a proton from HCl. Therefore, Cl – is a conjugate base of HCl and HCl is the conjugate acid of base Cl – . Similarly, H 2 O is a conjugate base of an acid H 3 O + and H 3 O + is a conjugate acid of base H 2 O.','[{"s": "It can be seen in the above equation, that water acts as a base because it accepts the proton.", "t": "text"}, {"s": "The species H", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "3", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "O", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "+", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "is produced when water accepts a proton from HCl.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "Therefore, Cl", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is a conjugate base of HCl and HCl is the conjugate acid of base Cl", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". Similarly, H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "O is a conjugate base of an acid H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "O", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+", "t": "text"}, {"s": "is a conjugate acid of base H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "O.", "t": "text"}]','marked','["71159"]',NULL),
