(10933,43,919,'paragraph',NULL,'K b = 1.77 × 10 –5 ) and therefore remains almost unionised in solution. This results in increased of H + ion concentration in solution making the solution acidic. Thus, the pH of NH 4 Cl solution in water is less than 7.','[{"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "b", "t": "text"}, {"s": "= 1.77 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–5", "t": "text"}, {"s": ") and therefore remains almost unionised in solution. This results in increased of H", "t": "text"}, {"s": "+", "t": "text"}, {"s": "ion concentration in solution making the solution acidic. Thus, the pH of NH", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "Cl solution in water is less than 7.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(10934,43,920,'paragraph',NULL,'Consider the hydrolysis of CH 3 COONH 4 salt formed from weak acid and weak base. The ions formed undergo hydrolysis as follow:','[{"s": "Consider the hydrolysis of CH", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "COONH", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "salt formed from weak acid and weak base. The ions formed undergo hydrolysis as follow:", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
