(10976,43,962,'paragraph',NULL,'We call K sp the solubility product constant or simply solubility product . The experimental value of K sp –10 . This means that for solid barium sulphate in equilibrium with its saturated solution, the product of the concentrations of barium and sulphate ions is equal to its solubility product constant. The concentrations of the two ions will be equal to the molar solubility of the barium sulphate. If molar solubility is S, then','[{"s": "We call", "t": "text"}, {"s": "K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "sp", "t": "text"}, {"s": "the", "t": "text"}, {"s": "solubility product constant", "t": "text"}, {"s": "or simply", "t": "text"}, {"s": "solubility product", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". The experimental value of", "t": "text"}, {"s": "K", "t": "text"}, {"s": "sp", "t": "text"}, {"s": "", "t": "br"}, {"s": "–10", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". This means that for solid barium sulphate in equilibrium with its saturated solution, the product of the concentrations of barium and sulphate ions is equal to its solubility product constant. The concentrations of the two ions will be equal to the molar solubility of the barium sulphate. If molar solubility is S, then", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
