(10980,43,966,'paragraph',NULL,'A salt may give on dissociation two or more than two anions and cations carrying different charges. For example, consider a salt like zirconium phosphate of molecular formula (Zr 4+ ) 3 (PO 4 3– ) 4 . It dissociates into 3 zirconium cations of charge +4 and 4 phosphate anions of charge –3. If the molar solubility of zirconium phosphate is S, then it can be seen from the stoichiometry of the compound that','[{"s": "A salt may give on dissociation two or more than two anions and cations carrying different charges.", "t": "hl"}, {"s": "For example, consider a salt like", "t": "text"}, {"s": "zirconium phosphate", "t": "text"}, {"s": "of molecular formula (Zr", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4+", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3", "t": "text"}, {"s": "(PO", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": "3–", "t": "text"}, {"s": ")", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". It dissociates into 3 zirconium cations of charge +4 and 4 phosphate anions of charge –3. If the molar solubility of zirconium phosphate is S, then it can be seen from the stoichiometry of the compound that", "t": "text"}]','marked','["71230"]',NULL),
