(11221,43,1207,'paragraph',NULL,'7.73 The concentration of sulphide ion in 0.1M HCl solution saturated with hydrogen sulphide is 1.0 × 10 –19 M. If 10 mL of this is added to 5 mL of 0.04 M solution of the following: FeSO 4 , MnCl 2 , ZnCl 2 and CdCl 2 . in which of these solutions precipitation will take place?','[{"s": "7.73 The concentration of sulphide ion in 0.1M HCl solution saturated with hydrogen sulphide is 1.0 × 10", "t": "text"}, {"s": "–19", "t": "text"}, {"s": "M. If 10 mL of this is added to 5 mL of 0.04 M solution of the following: FeSO", "t": "text"}, {"s": "4", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", MnCl", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ", ZnCl", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": "and CdCl", "t": "text"}, {"s": "2", "t": "text"}, {"s": ". in which of these solutions precipitation will take place?", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(11222,43,1208,'paragraph',NULL,'SUGGESTED ACTIVITIES FOR STUDENTS REGARDING THIS UNIT','[{"s": "SUGGESTED ACTIVITIES FOR STUDENTS REGARDING THIS UNIT", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(11223,43,1209,'paragraph',NULL,'(a) The student may use pH paper in determining the pH of fresh juices of various vegetables and fruits, soft drinks, body fluids and also that of water samples available.','[{"s": "(a) The student may use pH paper in determining the pH of fresh juices of various vegetables and fruits, soft drinks, body fluids and also that of water samples available.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(11224,43,1210,'paragraph',NULL,'(b) The pH paper may also be used to determine the pH of different salt solutions and from that he/she may determine if these are formed from strong/weak acids and bases.','[{"s": "(b) The pH paper may also be used to determine the pH of different salt solutions and from that he/she may determine if these are formed from strong/weak acids and bases.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(11225,43,1211,'paragraph',NULL,'(c) They may prepare some buffer solutions by mixing the solutions of sodium acetate and acetic acid and determine their pH using pH paper.','[{"s": "(c) They may prepare some buffer solutions by mixing the solutions of sodium acetate and acetic acid and determine their pH using pH paper.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(11226,43,1212,'paragraph',NULL,'(d) They may be provided with different indicators to observe their colours in solutions of varying pH.','[{"s": "(d) They may be provided with different indicators to observe their colours in solutions of varying pH.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(11227,43,1213,'paragraph',NULL,'(e) They may perform some acid-base titrations using indicators.','[{"s": "(e) They may perform some acid-base titrations using indicators.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(11228,43,1214,'paragraph',NULL,'(f) They may observe common ion effect on the solubility of sparingly soluble salts.','[{"s": "(f) They may observe common ion effect on the solubility of sparingly soluble salts.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
(11229,43,1215,'paragraph',NULL,'(g) If pH meter is available in their school, they may measure the pH with it and compare the results obtained with that of the pH paper.','[{"s": "(g) If pH meter is available in their school, they may measure the pH with it and compare the results obtained with that of the pH paper.", "t": "text"}]',NULL,NULL,NULL),
